@startuml
title L2-016 - Maintain manual metadata without losing user changes
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}

actor "Library owner" as actor
box "Frontend - Loupe application / domain / api" #E0F2FE
participant "MetadataEditor" as page
participant "MetadataService" as client
end box
box "Backend - Loupe API application" #D1FADF
participant "MetadataController" as controller
end box
box "Backend - Loupe Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
participant "UpdateMetadataCommandHandler" as handler
participant "MetadataState" as entity
end box
box "Backend - Loupe Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
database "Library store" as db
end box
actor -> page : Maintain manual metadata without losing user changes
page -> client : description/summary?, activeTags, version
client -> controller : PUT /api/metadata/{kind}/{id}
note over controller : API middleware authenticates; controller binds only
controller -> handler : MediatR dispatch UpdateMetadataCommand
handler -> db : Load / validate owner-scoped state before side effects
db --> handler : Owned state or unavailable result
handler -> entity : Normalize manual values and categories [L2-016]
opt description cleared
handler -> entity : Suppress old machine draft; advance decision revision
end
handler -> db : Conditional active metadata update + source revision + work intent
alt competing manual edit
db --> handler : 409; existing values preserved
else save accepted
db --> handler : Immediate keyword/filter fields; semantic pending
end
note over entity : AI appends suggestions only; never restores cleared active values
handler --> controller : 200 metadata/version or retained-input conflict
controller --> client : Typed HTTP response / ProblemDetails
client --> page : Update state signals
page --> actor : Saved / loaded state or retained-input error
@enduml
